  "text" : "A dot product tells you how much two vectors point the same way.\nIt's a way to measure similarity in AI models.\nThe way the math works is you multiply pairwise and then sum.\n1, 2, 3, dot, 4, minus 1, 0.\nThat's 4, minus 2, 0, sum, 2.\nWatch the number as this arrow turns.\nPointing the same direction is positive.\nAt 90 degrees, they're perpendicular, orthogonal, exactly 0.\nNo overlap at all.\nPointing opposite is negative.\nwhy it's everywhere in AI. Embeddings that mean similar things point in similar\ndirections, and the dot product is how you check. It's also the core of\nattention."
